    "Reason : 1 - REFUSE � The proposal fails to comply with the terms of Schedule 2, Part 1, Class A.1, Clauses g, i, j and ja of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended) because:\r\n\r\nThe proposed extension adjoins to non-original side and rear additions which, cumulatively, exceed the above requirements by having a depth of more than six metres, an eaves height of more than three metres within two metres of the boundary, and a total height of more than four metres. The cumulative extensions would also project past an original side wall of the house and have a width greater than half that of the original dwellinghouse and, cumulatively, would be more than a storey in height. \r\n"
